  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TZ HAKIZETU-Living Better Today</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The grant applied by Hakizetu Organization aims to support young mothers from disadvantage background with skills of vocational training where 15 young women and girls will enroll to a one year intensive training on garment making and designing and supported to establish fashion business of ready made garment cloths, 40 young women and girls will be supported with training on small business start-up while also supported to establish or strengthen their business with an opportunity to accessing 6 months business mentorship. Also 3200 young women will be trained on sexual reproductive health rights including family planning and violence prevention through using &#x201c;Process Oriented Approach&#x201d; (POA) and self-defense approach. Self-Defense gives women and girls power to choose how to respond to violence, without judgment or victim blaming. It empowers them to be in command of their minds, body, and spirit. It teaches them how to allow and to live their lives boldly and freely without fear. Hakizetu is planning to conduct those activities in order to give young women and girls an economic freedom and support them to engage direct in decision making especially on issues that affect their lives directly.

The primary goal for this project is to Create access to social and economic opportunities through empowering young Women and girls. Furthermore, this approved project aims to promote young women and girls&#x2019; economic empowerment through gender mainstreaming. This will be done through capacity building, skills trainings and provision of seed capital and supporting themto access seed capital and soft loan to other financial institutions in order for them to be economic independent, entrepreneurshipskills training, and business mentorship for a period of up to 6 months will enable them to recover from economic impact of Covid-19.

In order to achieve the intended results, the project aims to implement the following activities:
1. Garment Making and Designing Training.
2. Business Start-up and strengthen Training to 30 Young Women and Girls
3. Community Mobilization sessions on SRHR and Economic rights through using Process Oriented Approach (POA)
4. Attend Voice Linking and Learning events
5. External Evaluation</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hakizetu is a non-governmental and young people led organization that was founded in 2015 and legally registered in 2016 to operatein Tanzania mainland. Hakizetu is working on preventing gender-based violence against young women, adolescents and youth including sexual violence, child marriage and teenage pregnancy. Hakizetu also works on promoting accessibility of right and quality Sexual Reproductive Health services and information among women, adolescents and youth including accessibility of youth friendly health services. Hakizetu also works on empowering economically young women and youth, survivors of violence through provision of vocational skills, entrepreneurship skill, business mentorship and seed capital for business start-up and strengtheningCurrently Hakizetu is implementing its activities in Geita, Shinyanga, Mwanza and Arusha regions of Tanzania with 3 offices (Branches) in Mwanza and Arusha
Tanzania. Hakizetu is a Swahili word, which literally means &#x2018;Our rights&#x2019; in English. Hakizetu wasfounded by 5 persons; 1 man and 4 women who felt compelled to undertake and implement the goal and objectives under the core values of the organization towards positive action to enhance the young women and girls, children and youth&#x2019; voices to access theiruniversal human rights to equity, equality, justice and safety.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Hakizetu</narrative>
